# Field table: Aquis Stock Exchange (AQSE) multicast market data: real-time
# feed, snapshot feed and TCP replay service of the AQSE trading platform.
#
# Document (public):
#   AQSE  Aquis Stock Exchange Multicast Market Data Technical Specification,
#         version 1.2.3, April 2024 (1.2.3 changed branding only against 1.2.2,
#         February 2021).
#         https://aqx-web-prod-s3-public-read.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/Aquis_Stock_Exchange_Multicast_Market_Data_Specification_v1_2_3_2024_fc07d16378.pdf
# Citations: AQSE p.<PDF page> (the printed page number is the PDF page
# minus 4), section <n>.
#
# Same data types, packet structure and 6-byte header as the Aquis Exchange
# feed (aquis_md.tbl): little endian, 1-byte packing, char(n) NUL padded,
# price 5 implied decimals, timestamp ns since the Unix epoch (AQSE p.9,
# 3.1-3.2; p.10, 3.3.1). The message set and several layouts differ (no
# mdFlags, no pubTimestamp, no Segment MIC, quotes and trade reports), so the
# venue has its own table and namespace.
@venue aqse
@endian little
@pad nul
@type u8 uint
@type u16 uint
@type u32 uint
@type u64 uint
@type price uint
@type timestamp uint
@type char char

### pkt::from_aqse

MessageType - 0 0 # PacketHeader: first byte of every multicast packet (AQSE p.9, 3.2)
@size 1
messageCount u8 0 1 # Number of messages in this packet

### md::from_aqse
@type_code uint 1

MessageType 1 0 1 # Heartbeat: header only; seqNo is the next business message expected and is not consumed (AQSE p.10, 3.3.2; p.7, 2.1)
@size 6
length u8 1 1 # 6
seqNo u32 2 4 # Next expected business sequence number

MessageType 2 0 1 # OrderAdd: visible order quantity posted to the book; continuous trading only (AQSE p.10, 3.4.1)
@size 33
length u8 1 1 # 33
seqNo u32 2 4 # Sequence number in the stream for the current trading day
securityID u16 6 2 # Numeric identifier of the security
side u8 8 1 # 1 buy, 2 sell
quantity u32 9 4 # Shares added to the book
price price 13 8 # Price of the order
orderRef u32 21 4 # Unique order reference number for the day
timestamp timestamp 25 8 # Time of this market data event

MessageType 3 0 1 # OrderCancel: a visible order removed from the book; continuous trading only (AQSE p.11, 3.4.2)
@size 20
length u8 1 1 # 20
seqNo u32 2 4 # Sequence number in the stream for the current trading day
securityID u16 6 2 # Numeric identifier of the security
orderRef u32 8 4 # Unique order reference number for the day
timestamp timestamp 12 8 # Time of this market data event

MessageType 4 0 1 # OrderModify: price and/or quantity changed; quantity down keeps priority, otherwise re-ordered; continuous trading only (AQSE p.11, 3.4.3)
@size 32
length u8 1 1 # 32
seqNo u32 2 4 # Sequence number in the stream for the current trading day
securityID u16 6 2 # Numeric identifier of the security
quantity u32 8 4 # Shares remaining in the book
price price 12 8 # Price of the order
orderRef u32 20 4 # Unique order reference number for the day
timestamp timestamp 24 8 # Time of this market data event

MessageType 20 0 1 # QuoteAddReplace: a market maker's two-sided quote for a security (AQSE p.11-12, 3.4.4)
@size 42
length u8 1 1 # 42
seqNo u32 2 4 # Sequence number in the stream for the current trading day
traderID u16 6 2 # Market maker quoting (Trader Definition)
securityID u16 8 2 # Numeric identifier of the security
bidQuantity u32 10 4 # Bid shares available
bidPrice price 14 8 # Bid price
offerQuantity u32 22 4 # Offer shares available
offerPrice price 26 8 # Offer price
timestamp timestamp 34 8 # Time of this market data event

MessageType 21 0 1 # QuoteCancel: a quote removed (AQSE p.12, 3.4.5)
@size 18
length u8 1 1 # 18
seqNo u32 2 4 # Sequence number in the stream for the current trading day
traderID u16 6 2 # Originator of the quote
securityID u16 8 2 # Numeric identifier of the security
timestamp timestamp 10 8 # Time of this market data event

MessageType 5 0 1 # Trade: an order traded, partly or fully; also the AoD trade (AQSE p.12, 3.4.6; p.17, 3.5.2)
@size 41
length u8 1 1 # 41
seqNo u32 2 4 # Sequence number in the stream for the current trading day
securityID u16 6 2 # Numeric identifier of the security
tradeType u8 8 1 # 1 visible, 2 hidden or reserve, 6 AoD, 8 Trade Capture Report (AQSE p.19, 3.6.2)
quantity u32 9 4 # Shares traded
price price 13 8 # Execution price
orderRef u32 21 4 # Order reference, for tradeType 1 (visible)
tradeRef u32 25 4 # Trade reference; not unique for the day, with timestamp it is (AQSE p.6, 2.1)
timestamp timestamp 29 8 # Time of this market data event
BinaryMMT u32 37 4 # MMT flags (AQSE p.17-19, 3.6.1)

MessageType 25 0 1 # TradeReport: a new trade report submitted to AQSE (AQSE p.13, 3.4.7)
@size 45
length u8 1 1 # 45
seqNo u32 2 4 # Sequence number in the stream for the current trading day
securityID u16 6 2 # Numeric identifier of the security
tradeType u8 8 1 # See AQSE p.19, 3.6.2
quantity u32 9 4 # Shares traded
price price 13 8 # Execution price
tradeRef u32 21 4 # Trade report reference number
timestamp timestamp 25 8 # System received timestamp
BinaryMMT u32 33 4 # MMT flags
transactTime timestamp 37 8 # Time the transaction occurred

MessageType 26 0 1 # TradeReportModify: a published trade report modified, up to five business days later; preceded by a Trade Report Cancel of the original (AQSE p.13, 3.4.8)
@size 57
length u8 1 1 # 57
seqNo u32 2 4 # Sequence number in the stream for the current trading day
securityID u16 6 2 # Numeric identifier of the security
tradeType u8 8 1 # See AQSE p.19, 3.6.2
quantity u32 9 4 # Shares traded
price price 13 8 # Execution price
tradeRef u32 21 4 # Trade report reference number
timestamp timestamp 25 8 # System received timestamp
BinaryMMT u32 33 4 # MMT flags
transactTime timestamp 37 8 # Time the transaction occurred
origTradeRef u32 45 4 # Reference of the previous accepted trade report message
origTimestamp timestamp 49 8 # Timestamp of the previous accepted trade report message

MessageType 27 0 1 # TradeReportCancel: a published trade report cancelled, up to five business days later (AQSE p.14, 3.4.9)
@size 65
length u8 1 1 # 65
seqNo u32 2 4 # Sequence number in the stream for the current trading day
origSecurityID u16 6 2 # Security of the previous accepted trade report message
origTradeType u8 8 1 # Trade type of the previous accepted trade report message
origQuantity u32 9 4 # Shares of the previous accepted trade report message
origPrice price 13 8 # Price of the previous accepted trade report message
tradeRef u32 21 4 # Trade report reference number
timestamp timestamp 25 8 # System received timestamp
BinaryMMT u32 33 4 # MMT flags
transactTime timestamp 37 8 # Time the transaction occurred
origTradeRef u32 45 4 # Reference of the previous accepted trade report message
origTimestamp timestamp 49 8 # Timestamp of the previous accepted trade report message
origTransactTime timestamp 57 8 # Time the original transaction occurred

MessageType 6 0 1 # TradeBust: a trade declared erroneous; order generated trades only (AQSE p.14-15, 3.4.10)
@size 36
length u8 1 1 # 36
seqNo u32 2 4 # Sequence number in the stream for the current trading day
securityID u16 6 2 # Numeric identifier of the security
quantity u32 8 4 # Shares of the original trade
price price 12 8 # Execution price of the original trade
tradeRef u32 20 4 # Trade reference of the busted trade
timestamp timestamp 24 8 # Time of this market data event
BinaryMMT u32 32 4 # MMT flags

MessageType 22 0 1 # SecurityStatistics: opening and closing prices (AQSE p.15, 3.4.11; p.7, 2.1)
@size 25
length u8 1 1 # 25
seqNo u32 2 4 # Sequence number in the stream for the current trading day
securityID u16 6 2 # Numeric identifier of the security
price price 8 8 # Price
priceType u8 16 1 # 2 opening price, 5 closing price
timestamp timestamp 17 8 # Time of this market data event

MessageType 23 0 1 # TraderDefinition: a quote originator; pre-market (AQSE p.15, 3.4.12)
@size 24
length u8 1 1 # 24
seqNo u32 2 4 # Sequence number in the stream for the current trading day
traderID u16 6 2 # Numeric identifier of the trader
senderID char 8 16 # SenderID of the trader

MessageType 7 0 1 # TickTableData: one band of a dynamic tick table, or a static tick; pre-market (AQSE p.15-16, 3.4.13)
@size 33
length u8 1 1 # 33
seqNo u32 2 4 # Sequence number in the stream for the current trading day
tickTableID u8 6 1 # Identifier of the tick table or static tick
name char 7 10 # Short name
threshold price 17 8 # Price from which this tick size applies
tickSize price 25 8 # Price increment

MessageType 8 0 1 # SecurityDefinition: a security on this feed; pre-market, rarely intraday (AQSE p.16, 3.4.14)
@size 34
length u8 1 1 # 34
seqNo u32 2 4 # Sequence number in the stream for the current trading day
securityID u16 6 2 # Numeric identifier of the security
UMTF char 8 6 # Not applicable to AQSE
ISIN char 14 12 # ISIN
currency char 26 3 # Trading currency
MIC char 29 4 # MIC of the market of listing
tickTableId u8 33 1 # The security's tick table

MessageType 9 0 1 # SecurityStatus: trading status of a security or of its market changed (AQSE p.16-17, 3.4.15)
@size 18
length u8 1 1 # 18
seqNo u32 2 4 # Sequence number in the stream for the current trading day
securityID u16 6 2 # Numeric identifier of the security
tradingStatus u8 8 1 # 1 Active, 2 Halted, 3 Suspended
marketFlags u8 9 1 # Bit 0 continuous trading open (AoD available), bit 3 pre phase; with bit 0: 0/1 pre-open, 1/0 open, 1/1 pre-close, 0/0 closed
timestamp timestamp 10 8 # Time of this market data event

MessageType 17 0 1 # AoDUpdate: indicative price and matched volume during an AoD; the first one starts the auction (AQSE p.17, 3.5.1)
@size 28
length u8 1 1 # 28
seqNo u32 2 4 # Sequence number in the stream for the current trading day
securityID u16 6 2 # Numeric identifier of the security
indicativePrice price 8 8 # Indicative auction price
matchVol u32 16 4 # Indicative matched volume
timestamp timestamp 20 8 # Time of this market data event

### snap::from_aqse
@type_code uint 1

MessageType 10 0 1 # SnapshotStart: first message of each snapshot, every 10 s; continuous trading only (AQSE p.20, 3.7.1; p.7, 2.2)
@size 20
length u8 1 1 # 20
seqNo u32 2 4 # Not described for the snapshot feed
streamSeqNo u32 6 4 # Sequence number of the last continuous-stream message the snapshot relates to
securityCount u16 10 2 # Securities reported in this snapshot
timestamp timestamp 12 8 # Time of this snapshot

MessageType 11 0 1 # BookStatus: status of one security and the number of its open orders (AQSE p.20, 3.7.2)
@size 28
length u8 1 1 # 28
seqNo u32 2 4 # Not described for the snapshot feed
securityID u16 6 2 # Numeric identifier of the security
tradingStatus u8 8 1 # As Security Status (the spec says "Section 3.4.13", which is Tick Table Data)
marketFlags u8 9 1 # As Security Status
entries u16 10 2 # Open orders in the book; that many Book Entry messages follow
closingBuyQty u32 12 4 # Total buy quantity during the closing market, otherwise 0
closingSellQty u32 16 4 # Total sell quantity during the closing market, otherwise 0
indicativePrice price 20 8 # Indicative auction price

MessageType 12 0 1 # BookEntry: one open order; price-time priority for one side, then the other (AQSE p.21, 3.7.3)
@size 25
length u8 1 1 # 25
seqNo u32 2 4 # Not described for the snapshot feed
securityID u16 6 2 # Numeric identifier of the security
Side u8 8 1 # 1 buy, 2 sell
quantity u32 9 4 # Open shares
Price price 13 8 # Price of the order
orderRef u32 21 4 # Unique order reference number for the day

### replay::to_aqse
@type_code uint 1

MessageType 13 0 1 # Login: first message on a replay connection (AQSE p.21, 3.8.1)
@size 26
length u8 1 1 # 26
seqNo u32 2 4 # 0; ignored by AQSE (AQSE p.21, 3.8)
username char 6 10 # As assigned by AQSE
password char 16 10 # As assigned by AQSE

MessageType 14 0 1 # ReplayRequest: request one message or a range (AQSE p.21-22, 3.8.2)
@size 14
length u8 1 1 # 14
seqNo u32 2 4 # 0; ignored by AQSE
beginSeqNo u32 6 4 # Stream seqNo of the first message requested
endSeqNo u32 10 4 # Stream seqNo of the last message requested

### replay::from_aqse
@type_code uint 1
@include md::from_aqse

MessageType 15 0 1 # ReplayResponse: Login accepted, or a Replay Request refused (AQSE p.22, 3.8.3)
@size 7
length u8 1 1 # 7
seqNo u32 2 4 # 0
responseCode u8 6 1 # 0 Login successful, 1 bad beginSeqNo, 2 bad endSeqNo

### end
